      "note": "'ཆུ་ཚོད་{h}' on the hour; 'ཆུ་ཚོད་{h}་དང་སྐར་མ་<minutes>' additive (Tibetan-family 'hour X and minute N'); 'ཆུ་ཚོད་{h}་དང་ཕྱེད' for half past. Minute numerals use the written decimal forms (བཅོ་ལྔ, ཉི་ཤུ, ཉེར་ལྔ, སོ་ལྔ, བཞི་བཅུ, ཞེ་ལྔ, ལྔ་བཅུ, ང་ལྔ). Doubts: Dzongkha colloquial may prefer a subtractive 'to' form for :45–:55 and the vigesimal (ཁལ) counting in speech; tsheg-joined spelling chosen over the space-separated style used elsewhere in the file for digits."
